Report this machine's connection, token storage and expiry, default target and backend.
Works offline: never contacts the server, accesses the keychain, reads or unlocks a stored token, prompts, or changes files. It cannot detect server-side revocation.
Passphrase storage is reported as locked unless THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN is set, even when THE_AGENT_CLI_PASSPHRASE is available. Expired tokens require reconnecting.

Example report (macOS, clock at 2026-11-14 10:21):
Connected as Example User (workstation)
  Device ID: 6b8f0d3e-2a1c-4e55-9a37-0c1d2e3f4a5b
  Token: macOS Keychain, expires 2027-02-14 10:21 (in 3 months)
  Default chat: 3f2a9c1e7b6d4a58b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7 (telegram · Example Chat, private)
  Backend: http://localhost

Use agent-cli connect <KEY> to connect this machine.

Usage: agent-cli status

Flags:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli status

Environment: THE_AGENT_CLI_HOME, THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL, THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_CHAT, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_PLATFORM
Exit codes: 0 locally connected · 1 local state unusable · 2 usage or default validation error · 3 not connected, locked, expired or invalid environment token
